From e1501792383bb7a8012a3afeb3281141f424dbae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zach Aw <zachary_aw@outlook.sg>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 14:15:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] vulkan: add GGML_OP_DSV4_HC_EXPAND kernel

Hyperconnection expand for DeepSeek-V4:

  out[d, dst_hc, t] = block_out[d, t] * post[dst_hc, t]
                    + sum_src_hc comb[dst_hc, src_hc, t] * residual[d, src_hc, t]

One thread per output element over ggml_nelements(dst), walking the flat
index in the same order as ggml_compute_forward_dsv4_hc_expand
(ggml-cpu/ops.cpp) and kernel_dsv4_hc_expand (ggml-metal.metal), with the
same comb indexing (dim0 = dst_hc, dim1 = src_hc) and the same ascending
src_hc accumulation order.

All four sources are read through per-tensor element strides taken from the
tensors themselves, so the model's n_tokens == 1 decode path - where post
and comb are strided views at non-zero offsets into the sinkhorn split -
needs no ggml_cont. A dedicated push-constant struct carries the strides
plus the five misalignment offsets.

Wired through the generic vk_op_f32 path (4 srcs -> 5 bindings), reusing
the elements/dispatch group of the elementwise ops (512x512xZ split), with
supports_op mirroring the Metal gate, and test-backend-ops coverage:
canonical 7168x4 prefill, decode offset views, padded-stride views, odd
n_embd/n_hc, n_hc = 1 and 16, and a >262144-element z-split. 8/8 pass on
RADV GFX1151.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
